CHANGED: `Clash.Sized.Vector`'s indexing functions now use `Index` instead of `Enum` for their index arguments, making them total. This affects `(!!)`, `replace`, `gather`, `scatter`, `permute`, and `backpermute`, as well as `Clash.Sized.RTree`'s `indexTree` and `replaceTree`. Previously these accepted any `Enum`-typed index (e.g. `Int`), which silently allowed out-of-bounds values and made the functions partial. To convert an index explicitly, use `numConvert` (for numeric types) or the new `tagToIndex` (for enumerations / ADTs). The old `Enum`-based behavior remains available (but deprecated) under `indexEnum`, `replaceEnum`, `gatherEnum`, `scatterEnum`, `permuteEnum`, `backpermuteEnum`, `indexTreeEnum`, and `replaceTreeEnum`.
NEW: `Clash.Sized.Vector.tagToIndex` converts the constructor tag of an enumeration into an `Index` sized to the number of constructors, providing a safe, total way to index a vector with an ADT.
